bootstrap.Args() under the interpreter now returns the host bni's own argv (here 5 tokens: -I/path/-L/path/487.bn), not the program's: the progArgsAfterDash shim was removed, so a program reads its own args from os.Args() (bni installs them via os.SetArgs), and direct bootstrap.Args() intentionally diverges. Compiled mode returns the program args (0). Design: explorations/design-os-args-vm.md.
